In Zorin OS and DEll laptop

1) Step 1 — Open Terminal and install the required system software
Copy-paste this one command:>> sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip python3-venv ffmpeg portaudio19-dev
  -sudo apt update - Updates Zorin's list of available software packages.
  -sudo apt install - Installs the tools your voice-assistant needs:
  -ffmpeg- needed by whisper
  -portaudio- helps sounddevice communicate with microphone
  -python3-venv - creates seperate python environment
  -python3 - runs your python program

2)Step 2 — Put your Python file on the Zorin laptop
>>mkdir ~/GeminiVoiceAssistant                                   //Create a project folder:
>>cd ~/GeminiVoiceAssistant                                      //change directory
/home/YOUR_USERNAME/GeminiVoiceAssistant/voice_assistant.py

Step 3 — Create Python environment
Inside the project folder, make a seperate project python environment, all libraries will be installed inside it 
python3 -m venv venv

Then activate it:
source venv/bin/activate

Step 4 — Install everything your program needs , With (venv) active, run:
pip install numpy scipy sounddevice openai-whisper google-genai pyttsx3

   # Library	What it does in your project
   - sounddevice	🎤 Captures audio from the microphone
   - numpy	📊 Processes the microphone audio data and calculates volume/threshold
   - scipy	💾 Saves the recorded audio as a .wav file
   - openai-whisper	🗣️ Converts your recorded speech → text
   - google-genai	🧠 Sends your text to Gemini and gets the AI response
   - pyttsx3	🔊 Converts Gemini's text response → spoken audio
